# Trivy misconfiguration whitelist for the DigitalOcean Terraform root.
# Add one check ID per line to accept a HIGH/CRITICAL finding (with a reason).
# See the check ID in the Trivy CI output (the terraform job in ci.yml).
# Both the short (DIG-0001) and AVD (AVD-DIG-0001) ID forms are listed so the
# match is version-independent.

# DIG-0001 — unrestricted ingress. Accepted: this is a public web droplet, so
# HTTP/80 and HTTPS/443 are intentionally open to 0.0.0.0/0. SSH/22 is NOT open
# by default — it is gated by var.ssh_allowed_cidrs (set it per deploy). See
# digitalocean_firewall.web in network.tf.
DIG-0001
AVD-DIG-0001

# DIG-0003 — unrestricted egress. Accepted: a general-purpose host needs
# outbound internet (package updates, API calls, OTLP export, etc.).
DIG-0003
AVD-DIG-0003
